<title>CROATIA: Croatia, India initial air traffic agreement.</title>
<headline>Croatia, India initial air traffic agreement.</headline>
<dateline>ZAGREB 1997-01-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Croatia and India on Tuesday initialled an agreement to regulate air traffic between the two countries, state news agency Hina reported.</p>
<p>The agreement is to be signed and enforced in the spring, when national airlines should agree on its details, Hina said.</p>
<p>It also said Air India already expressed interest in flying to Croatia as it planned to extend its traffic in central Europe.</p>
<p>The deal should boost economic and tourist cooperation and open up new possibilities for investment of Indian capital into Croatia, Hina quoted Croatia's assistant air traffic minister Zvonimir Vedris as saying.</p>
<p>-- Zagreb newsroom, 385-1-4557075</p>
